  "$comment": "Static, committed dataset. trueAreaKm2 is total area (land + inland water) per the CIA World Factbook. `id` is the numeric ISO 3166-1 / M49 code used as the feature id in world-atlas countries-110m.json. Nothing here is fetched at build or run time. Countries whose Natural Earth outline covers territory the quoted area excludes (France with its overseas departments, Norway with Svalbard) are deliberately left out, so that what is drawn and what is measured are the same country. Every entry is checked at build time: an outline that disagrees with its quoted area by more than 8 per cent fails the build, because the Equal Earth panel draws its areas from that outline and would then contradict the figure printed under it. That rule is what excludes Morocco (Western Sahara), Somalia (Somaliland), Pakistan (Kashmir), Saudi Arabia, Ecuador, Bangladesh and Yemen. Nothing below about 145,000 sq km is included either: the 110m atlas draws countries that small as unrecognisable polygons once a pair of them is scaled up to fill a panel.",
